ensitive  information like PII data of our  customers and combining those three  classifications together we created a  convention how we are naming our data  sets so data set in the quick query is  an aggregation of DB objects views and  tables and it has been mentioned but by  devil but just me repeat you grant  accesses on data set level so basically  you grant access to every single table  and viewed there is there is in this  particular data set so that's why let's  take a look on the example for example  the second data set order details it  means that we have information about  orders their data is not derived so the  information are not blended with  different systems it's purely about  orders and restricted so no PII inside  everyone the organization can use it so  this is how by just taking a look on the  name of the data set you know more or  less what is inside so this is basically  how we are governing our data how we are  loading the data to our alag and how we  are controlling that and transforming  our data if you are interested in  building data legs on GCP i would  recommend taking a look on materials  linked here for example article or some  QuickStart guides if you are not very  familiar with bigquery there is quite a  lot of resources courser also study it's  a lot of materials and there are also  some related sessions during this  conference so if this is something that  interests you I would recommend to join  them just letting you know that my  colleagues from Okada are also  delivering two sessions so if you are  interested for example how we are doing  machine learning just after plant there  is one session about building our cloud  ml infrastructure and on first there  there's another how we use AI to  leverage retail business so that's  basically all thank you it was a  pleasure to have a chance to talk to you  [Music]
 

